Thought: The proton NMR spectra provide valuable information about the hydrogen environment in the molecule. The presence of a singlet at 3.81 ppm suggests a methoxy group (OCH3). The triplets at 2.58 ppm and 2.84 ppm indicate the presence of two CH2 groups, likely in an aliphatic chain. The aromatic protons appear as doublets of doublets at 7.17 ppm and 7.93 ppm, suggesting a para-substituted benzene ring. I will now check the carbon NMR spectra to confirm the presence of these groups and further refine the structure.
