Action Input: {}

Thought: The carbon NMR spectra show signals that are consistent with the presence of a methoxy group (52.24 ppm), two aliphatic CH2 groups (43.47 ppm and 38.60 ppm), and aromatic carbons (129.70 ppm, 129.01 ppm, 131.87 ppm). The signal at 166.40 ppm suggests the presence of a carbonyl group, likely an amide or ester. Based on the NMR data and the molecular formula, the structure is likely to be an aromatic amide or ester with a methoxy group. I will now compare the NMR data with the possible isomers to identify the correct structure.
